Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: unicorn: retain the OEM amplifier bus rate

The OEM live tree leaves SE15's bus rate unspecified. Its i2c-msm-geni
probe defaults to 400 kHz, whereas upstream i2c-qcom-geni defaults to
100 kHz. At 100 kHz, the 20420-byte CS35L41 PM firmware region alone needs
at least 1.84 seconds, exceeding upstream's one-second transfer timeout.
Both amplifiers fail this firmware write on Unicorn. Make the original
400 kHz setting explicit; do not change calibration or amplifier protection.

Source: Unicorn OEM live i2c@880000 and OEM drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-msm-geni.c
probe default (gi2c->i2c_rsc.clk_freq_out = KHz(400)).

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-speakers.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-speakers.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-speakers.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-unicorn-speakers.dtsi
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 /* Unicorn CS35L41 amplifiers and protected 96 kHz TDM transport. */
 
 &i2c15 {
+	clock-frequency = <400000>;
 	status = "okay";
 
 	cs35l41_bottom: amplifier@40 {
